# Cloudflare Workers static-assets headers. Astro copies public/* verbatim
# into dist/, and Workers picks this file up from the asset directory root.
#
# Why this exists: the agent-facing endpoints (src/pages/**/index.md.ts,
# index.mdx.ts, llms.txt.ts) already return `charset=utf-8`, but the site
# builds with `output: "static"` — prerendering writes only the response
# body to disk and drops its headers. Cloudflare then infers the type from
# the extension alone, so `.md` went out as bare `text/markdown`. A browser
# rendering text/* with no declared charset falls back to the local default
# encoding, which turns every translated page into mojibake. HTML is immune
# because BaseLayout emits <meta charset="utf-8">; these files have no such
# fallback, so the charset has to come from the header.

/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8

/*.mdx
  Content-Type: text/mdx; charset=utf-8

/*.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
